// expect: runtime_error
// expect-error: E1004

// GAP — owner: 0.0.8 plan, step 1e (C4).
// Measured 2026-10-10 on the VM: `SoleInstance.measure(7)` prints 7, then
// `SoleInstance.measure("abc")` fails with error[E1004], a value of runtime
// type `String` at the `size(x)` in SoleInstance.measure.
//
// `measure<a: Sized>` should read `size` out of its `Sized` dictionary. The
// old dispatch path saw that `Sized<Int>` was the only instance in its module
// and called `__tc_Sized_Int_size` directly, so the `Sized<String>` instance
// this file adds is never used.
//
// The solver's evidence says the dictionary parameter, and since step 1d the
// Core path follows it (`--dump-core` shows `__dict_Sized.0`). The VM still
// compiles a module member through the CFG path, which has no scheme for it,
// so it keeps the direct call until 1e switches that path to evidence.

import SoleInstance

instance Sized<String> {
    fn size(s) { 100 }
}

fn main() with IO {
    print(SoleInstance.measure(7))
    print(SoleInstance.measure("abc"))
}
